---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LeadBlock from '../components/LeadBlock.astro';
---
<Base title="How Online A-level Tutoring Works: Booking, Lessons and Payment | aleveltutors.online" description="What happens when you book an online A-level tutor with us: the first conversation, weekly one-to-one lessons, recordings, and payment after each lesson.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
      <h1>How lessons work</h1>
      <p>Simple to arrange, easy to fit around school, and nothing to sign. Here is what to expect from the first message to the final exam.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Getting started</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Book or ask</h3><p>Choose a time in the tutor’s calendar from their subject page. If you’re unsure which tutor or how many lessons, message Tom first.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Secure the booking</h3><p>A card holds the booking. Nothing is charged until after the lesson.</p></li>
        <li><h3>A first conversation</h3><p>Before the first lesson, the tutor asks about the exam board, recent marks and what is causing most trouble, so no time is wasted.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Settle into a routine</h3><p>Most students keep the same weekly slot. Automatic reminders arrive before each lesson.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="block alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>In the lesson</h2></div>
      <div class="features">
        <div><h3>Working together on screen</h3><p>Lessons run on Zoom or Google Meet. Tutor and student see the same slides, diagrams and exam questions and can both write on them.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Real exam questions</h3><p>Lessons use past-paper questions and mark schemes, so students practise exactly what they will face and learn how answers are marked.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Bring the hard questions</h3><p>Students can send in questions from homework or tests that they got stuck on, and go through them in the next lesson.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Recorded for revision</h3><p>Every lesson is recorded and kept privately, so any explanation can be watched again before a test or in the run-up to the exams.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h2>Changing plans</h2>
      <p>There is no contract. A lesson can be moved with reasonable notice, lessons can pause over exams and holidays, and you can stop whenever you no longer need them. You only ever pay for lessons that have happened. See <a href="/fees/">fees</a> for the details.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <LeadBlock />
</Base>
